  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "            The verb 'estar' is irregular and used to indicate location or temporary states. \nIts present forms are: estoy (I am), estás (you are, informal singular), está (he/she/you formal is), estamos (we are), están (you plural/they are). \nSpanish also distinguishes between the formal second person pronoun 'usted' and the informal 'tú'. \nThese drills combine multiple-choice questions about pronoun-verb matching with response drills that practise selecting the correct location or choice.\n"
    }
